"yt":"CrFcxR4Y6C0","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Underground online","scene_id":30829935814163,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#underground-online","chapters":["Loops 2 · Cap. 10: Demonios de neón: la escena EDM, entre la resurrección de la cultura rave y la sumisión al mercado del pop"],"pages":[[2,352]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":352,"text":"…una nueva vía para explorar las posibilidades del pop entendido como la banda sonora de una adolescencia conflictiva: la popular estrella canadiense Carly Rae Jepsen colaboró con Danny L Harle en «Super Natural», y más tarde con Charli XCX en su mixtape Pop 2 (2017), producida por equipos de PC Music y en la que…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Career Launching Hit","body":"\"Call Me Maybe\" was Carly Rae Jepsen's breakthrough hit that, despite being her only major hit, \"set them up for a career.\" It was the 2012 Billboard Song of the Summer. \"And even when a song of summer is an act only major hit, it can still set them up for a career, like our beloved Carly Rae Jepsen.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Song(s) of the Summer Edition Part 2","url":null},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Song(s) of the Summer Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4ef50c30a1408dc292e4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Pop Dominance in 2010s","body":"Carly Rae Jepsen was among the pop artists who were part of the genre's significant rise in the 2010s, contributing to a period where pop, hip hop, and EDM collectively overshadowed rock music around 2011-2012. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"YouTube Discovery","body":"Carly Rae Jepsen's initial discovery occurred on YouTube, illustrating the digital shift in talent identification for A&R departments. \"Karly Rae Jebsen... they were all first found on YouTube.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Music Industry Glossary: Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5kPmqmbFfkY"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"American Music Award for New Artist of the Year (2012)","body":"Won.","year":2012,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1527196"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Teen Choice Awards (2012)","body":"Won.","year":2012,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q391629"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Billboard Music Awards (2013)","body":"Won.","year":2013,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q392565"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Canada's Walk of Fame (2013)","body":"Won.","year":2013,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q857933"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"NRJ Music Award for International Revelation of the Year (2013)","body":"Won.","year":2013,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3334531"}]}],"concerts":[{"kind":"concert","title":"Capital Summertime Ball 2015","body":null,"year":2015,"extra":null,"srcs":[]}],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":230407028954882,"type":"song","name":"C